<!-- SECTION: treasury.Principles -->
<section class="u-154 blk blk--cream" data-screen-label="Principles">
  <div class="eyebrow">The standing rules</div>
  <h2 class="sec">Rules that hold before a single dollar moves.</h2>
  <p class="lead">These apply from the first donation onward, whether or not anyone is watching.</p>
  <div class="prin">
    <div><h3><i></i>Receipts behind summaries</h3><p>Every expense retains an internal receipt and approval trail, even where public reporting is aggregated.</p></div>
    <div><h3><i></i>Money never buys influence</h3><p>Donations and in-kind support never buy conclusions, coverage, governance influence, votes, or preferential treatment.</p></div>
    <div><h3><i></i>No crypto treasury</h3><p>No cryptocurrency, no on-chain mechanics — segregated accounts under a confirmed lawful structure only.</p></div>
  </div>
  <p class="u-155">
    <span class="u-156"></span>
    <span>When reporting begins, figures will be summarized, with individual donor identities and security-sensitive line items redacted where appropriate — e.g. <span class="redact">██████████</span> — and totals preserved. Draft controls: <a class="u-1" href="/policies/financial-controls-donation/">POL-004</a>, <a class="u-1" href="/policies/conflict-of-interest/">POL-005</a>, <a class="u-1" href="/policies/in-kind-gift-acceptance/">POL-010</a> — public review drafts, not adopted.</span>
  </p>
</section>

